Share one copy of the bundled reference LAPACK between the two linalg modules.

numpy compiles lapack_lite/*.c -- the f2c'd reference BLAS and LAPACK used when
no optimised library is found -- directly into both `lapack_lite` and
`_umath_linalg`. As separate shared objects that is merely wasteful: each .so
carries its own copy. Linked statically into one interpreter it is fatal,
because scopy_, dgetrf_ and every other Fortran symbol is then defined twice in
the same module, and wasm-ld rejects it.

A static_library both modules link against is the same code with one
definition, and it drops the duplicated copy from the variant.

--- a/numpy/linalg/meson.build
+++ b/numpy/linalg/meson.build
@@ -16,13 +16,20 @@
   ]
 endif
 
-py.extension_module('lapack_lite',
+lapack_lite_lib = static_library('lapack_lite_shared_impl',
   [
-    'lapack_litemodule.c',
     python_xerbla_sources,
     lapack_lite_sources,
   ],
   dependencies: [np_core_dep, blas_dep, lapack_dep],
+)
+
+py.extension_module('lapack_lite',
+  [
+    'lapack_litemodule.c',
+  ],
+  dependencies: [np_core_dep, blas_dep, lapack_dep],
+  link_with: lapack_lite_lib,
   install: true,
   subdir: 'numpy/linalg',
 )
@@ -30,11 +37,9 @@
 py.extension_module('_umath_linalg',
   [
     'umath_linalg.cpp',
-    python_xerbla_sources,
-    lapack_lite_sources,
   ],
   dependencies: [np_core_dep, blas_dep, lapack_dep],
-  link_with: npymath_lib,
+  link_with: [npymath_lib, lapack_lite_lib],
   install: true,
   subdir: 'numpy/linalg',
 )
